    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for pet owners. When a `POST /api/owners` request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response now returns `ageBand` computed against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `birthDate` (ISO date) input to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.ageBand` (with the nested `AgeBandEnum`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date DATE` column) with getter/setter, so MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `ageBand(owner)` expression mapping: `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+); returns `null` when `birthDate` (or `registrationDate`) is absent.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (`ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the scripts).\n\nThe `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT` against a 2026 registration date) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
